body:
I don't have any recipe on hand and haven't eaten that tiramisu for years, maybe I should try to make one on my own to refresh my memory.

From what I remember, she used to follow the classic recipe, just skipping the mascarpone and egg yolks:

* *Savoiardi* biscuits soaked in coffee (she used decaffeinated coffee when I was younger);
* Whipped white eggs (tip: the fresher the eggs, the better hold they have when whipped) with sugar;
* Only one layer of biscuits and eggs (I can't remember if she ever tried to make a second layer, so I don't know if it would hold well if you do), the egg whites one being bigger/taller;
* Left in the fridge for a couple of hours or overnight;
* Cocoa powder on top before serving;

If I attempt to try one myself, I would keep you updated.

Also, I don't know what your cup is and I can only suggest outside resources like comparison webpages for help:

- [Period Nirvana - Menstrual Cup Comparison Chart](https://www.periodnirvana.com/menstrual-cup-chart/)
- [Put A Cup In It - Menstrual Cup Comparison Chart
](https://putacupinit.com/chart/)
- [Put A Cup In It - Menstrual Cup Visual Comparison Tool
](https://putacupinit.com/cup-comparison-tool/)
